      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__edge__functions_1ga4cb7ce244310b79ccc6f266256f5ff33" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>double *</type>
        <definition>double * ndxlEdgeState</definition>
        <argsstring>(NDXLEdge *_Edge)</argsstring>
        <name>ndxlEdgeState</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1aa30ac2f40da4dbe7d841088a78f957fe" kindref="member">NDXLEdge</ref> *</type>
          <declname>_Edge</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Provides direct access to the internal state vector of an edge. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Edge</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Target edge to see the state of.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>If _Edge is NULL, returns NULL, otherwise returns a pointer to the internal state vector or, when called from within a dynamics function, the current Runge–Kutta stage vector of _Edge.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>When called outside a dynamics function, this function returns a pointer to the edge&apos;s primary state vector. When called from within a dynamics function, it instead returns a pointer to the current intermediate Runge–Kutta stage vector. This behaviour allows the same function to be used for directly modifying an edge&apos;s state outside integration and accessing its current integration stage during dynamics evaluation.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>Direct modification of the returned vector is supported when it refers to the primary state vector. However, when called from within a dynamics function, the returned pointer refers to the intermediate Runge–Kutta stage vector. Modifying this vector directly is not intended for ordinary state updates and may interfere with the integration process.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Errors raised</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gaf6b8bdcb87bdd7944810152b510101e4" kindref="member">NDXL_ARG_ERR</ref> : _Edge is NULL.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="group__network__simulation" kindref="compound">Network Simulation</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
